// - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -
// Filename:	TS060 290-035 Polarise PCB.test
// Project:		CL Auto 2
// Author:      Foster & Freeman Ltd - Paul Evans
// Modified:    04/11/25
//
// Description: This script test the Driver and LED output for the Polariser.
// - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -

{0} force FAIL by default to avoid IMPORTANT message below.
#1: Equipment Setup 1.
a. Connect the Bus Priate and PSU to the test PC.
b. Connect the Bus Priate to the TE247 and set the pull-up shut to ON.
c. Connect the GND's to - of channel 1 on the PSU.
d. Connect the VPWR to + of channel 1 on the PSU.
e. Set the TENMA Programmable PSU power switch to on.
CLICK_OK:
CONNECT: TENMAPSU
IF_NOT:
GOTO: #1: 

#2: Equipment Setup 2 & Configure the PSU.
a. Enter the PCB serial number.
b. Connect the Bus Priate to the TE247 and set the pull-up shut to ON.
a. Connect the UUT to the test jig.
a. Connect the TE247 to the test jig.
b. Place the UUT inside the test box with camera.
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OUT0
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OCP1
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OCPSET1:0.750
COMMAND: TENMAPSU VSET1:12.00
COMMAND: TENMAPSU ISET1:0.500
CLICK_OK:

#3: Connect and Configure the Bus Pirate.
CONNECT: BUS_PIRATE
IF_NOT:
GOTO: #3:
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE m4
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE 3
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE W // sets the power rail to on, and drives a voltage to pin 5 C_PWR_ON
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE P

#4: Power on the PSU. 
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OUTCH1:1
CLICK_OK:

#5: ConfigMCGPIO
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE {0x4E 0x0A 0x80} {0x4E 0x00 0x07} {0x4E 0x10 0x00}
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE {0x4E 0x0A 0x00} //All Leds OFF
CLICK_OK:

#6: White LED Test – 
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE {0x4E 0x1A 0x01}//Set White
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE {0x4E 0x0A 0x08}//Brightness 100%
PASS_FAIL:
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE {0x4E 0x0A 0xB8}//Brightness 25%
PASS_FAIL:
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE {0x4E 0x0A 0xF8}//Brightness 1%
PASS_FAIL:
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE {0x4E 0x0A 0x88}//Brightness 50%
PASS_FAIL:
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE {0x4E 0x0A 0x00} //All Leds OFF

#7: IR LED Test – 
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE {0x4E 0x1A 0x02}// Set IR on
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE {0x4E 0x0A 0x08}//Brightness 100%
PASS_FAIL:
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE {0x4E 0x0A 0xB8}//Brightness 25%
PASS_FAIL:
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE {0x4E 0x0A 0xF8}//Brightness 1%
PASS_FAIL:
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE {0x4E 0x0A 0x88}//Brightness 50%
PASS_FAIL:
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE {0x4E 0x0A 0x00} //All Leds OFF

#8: POWER down process. 
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE m4
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE 3
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE W // sets the power rail to on, and drives a voltage to pin 5 C_PWR_ON
COMMAND: BUS_PIRATE P
DISCONNECT: BUS_PIRATE
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OUT0
DISCONNECT: TENMAPSU




#9: Test complete
IF: %FAILED% > 0
GOTO: #Failed:
ELSE: #Passed:

#Failed: A test failed.
a. This PCB has failed to pass all Tests
b. Check the Log file for more details on the failed test(s).
IMPORTANT: This PCB has failed to pass all Tests
//DISPLAY: test_failed.png
CLICK_OK:
GOTO: #QUIT:

#Passed: Test's Complete.
a. All tests instructions have been completed and a log file created.
b. Click OK to finish and power OFF.
//DISPLAY: AllTestsPassed.png
CLICK_OK:

#QUIT:
COMMAND: TENMAPSU VSET1:0.00
COMMAND: TENMAPSU ISET1:0.00
COMMAND: TENMAPSU VSET2:0.00
COMMAND: TENMAPSU ISET2:0.00
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OUT0
DISCONNECT: TENMAPSU
DISCONNECT: BUS_PIRATE
// End of file
// - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -